WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:02.887
Welcome.

2
00:00:02.907 --> 00:00:06.452
This is Session 3 of
our Catechism for Africa

3
00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:10.341
journey: I Believe —
Faith as Our Response.

4
00:00:10.361 --> 00:00:15.008
We are reading with the
Catechism of the Catholic Church,

5
00:00:15.028 --> 00:00:20.452
paragraphs one hundred and forty-two
to one hundred and seventy-five.

6
00:00:20.472 --> 00:00:25.702
Tonight's key question is simple
and searching: what is faith,

7
00:00:25.722 --> 00:00:30.045
and how is it different
from just having an opinion?

8
00:00:30.065 --> 00:00:34.258
At the Rite of Acceptance,
inquirers are asked what

9
00:00:34.278 --> 00:00:39.249
they seek from the Church,
and faith is the first answer.

10
00:00:39.269 --> 00:00:44.000
So let us begin where God
begins — with his word to us.

11
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.828
Faith always begins with God.

12
00:00:50.848 --> 00:00:53.760
Out of the fullness of his love,

13
00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:59.889
the invisible God addresses us as
friends and invites us into his company.

14
00:00:59.909 --> 00:01:03.353
That is revelation:
God speaks first.

15
00:01:03.373 --> 00:01:06.018
Our fitting response is faith.

16
00:01:06.038 --> 00:01:10.149
Faith is not an opinion
we hold about something.

17
00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:13.346
It is an answer we give to Someone.

18
00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:16.677
We freely entrust our
whole selves — mind

19
00:01:16.697 --> 00:01:20.408
and will — to the God
who reveals himself.

20
00:01:20.428 --> 00:01:24.739
When God speaks, he is
not selling us an idea.

21
00:01:24.759 --> 00:01:27.690
He is calling us into friendship.

22
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:38.317
We have already met our models of
faith, so this is only a short recap.

23
00:01:38.337 --> 00:01:42.491
Abraham is called the
father of all who believe.

24
00:01:42.511 --> 00:01:46.666
At God's word he left
his homeland and set out,

25
00:01:46.686 --> 00:01:49.831
without seeing the whole road ahead.

26
00:01:49.851 --> 00:01:53.467
He obeyed before he
understood every step.

27
00:01:53.487 --> 00:01:58.315
Faith begins by listening to
God and acting on his word,

28
00:01:58.335 --> 00:02:01.230
even when the map is incomplete.

29
00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.800
Mary shows the same trust.

30
00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.376
When the angel spoke,
she answered: let

31
00:02:11.396 --> 00:02:14.887
it be done to me
according to your word.

32
00:02:14.907 --> 00:02:17.812
Her whole life was a yes to God.

33
00:02:17.832 --> 00:02:20.413
Abraham and Mary both trust God's

34
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:23.598
word before they
understand everything.

35
00:02:23.618 --> 00:02:26.329
Their faith is not stubbornness.

36
00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:29.189
It is a living relationship with the

37
00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:32.460
God who speaks and
keeps his promises.

38
00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.390
So what is faith?

39
00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:43.099
The Catechism says it has two
sides that belong together.

40
00:02:43.119 --> 00:02:46.958
First, faith is personal
trust: we hold on

41
00:02:46.978 --> 00:02:51.078
to God himself — a
Person, not only an idea.

42
00:02:51.098 --> 00:02:53.891
Second, because we trust him,

43
00:02:53.911 --> 00:02:58.142
we freely accept as true
all that he has revealed.

44
00:02:58.162 --> 00:03:02.655
We believe what God says
because we trust who God is.

45
00:03:02.675 --> 00:03:05.009
For those already baptised,

46
00:03:05.029 --> 00:03:09.522
you may already have a strong
personal faith in Jesus.

47
00:03:09.542 --> 00:03:15.539
The new step is to receive the faith
of the Catholic Church as your own,

48
00:03:15.559 --> 00:03:19.397
including teachings you
may not yet know well.

49
00:03:19.417 --> 00:03:21.883
Honest questions are welcome.

50
00:03:21.903 --> 00:03:23.080
Bring them.

51
00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:32.464
Faith is a gift of God — a
supernatural virtue that he gives.

52
00:03:32.484 --> 00:03:36.247
And yet believing is
also a fully human act.

53
00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:40.553
It does not destroy our
freedom or our intelligence.

54
00:03:40.573 --> 00:03:43.358
God invites; he never forces.

55
00:03:43.378 --> 00:03:49.685
We already trust people every day: the
taxi driver at five in the morning,

56
00:03:49.705 --> 00:03:51.903
the doctor's prescription,

57
00:03:51.923 --> 00:03:55.817
the friend who holds our
savings in a stokvel.

58
00:03:55.837 --> 00:04:02.210
Faith in God is like this, but more
certain, because God cannot deceive.

59
00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:06.255
Christian faith is not a
charm against bad luck.

60
00:04:06.275 --> 00:04:09.080
It is trust in a loving Father.

61
00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:18.048
Faith is certain because it
rests on God, who cannot lie.

62
00:04:18.068 --> 00:04:20.756
It also seeks to understand more.

63
00:04:20.776 --> 00:04:24.694
Real science and faith
never contradict each other.

64
00:04:24.714 --> 00:04:27.340
Saint Augustine put it this way,

65
00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:33.678
preaching on the Gospel of John: do not
seek to understand in order to believe,

66
00:04:33.698 --> 00:04:36.570
but believe that you may understand.

67
00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:40.755
Understanding, he says,
is the reward of faith.

68
00:04:40.775 --> 00:04:43.524
His point is gentle and practical.

69
00:04:43.544 --> 00:04:48.016
Do not wait to understand
everything before you trust God.

70
00:04:48.036 --> 00:04:51.031
Trust, and understanding will come,

71
00:04:51.051 --> 00:04:54.620
step by step, in the
light of his truth.

72
00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.800
Faith is necessary for salvation.

73
00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.574
We can also lose it,
so we nourish it by

74
00:05:05.594 --> 00:05:09.690
the Word of God, by
prayer and by charity.

75
00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:14.630
In darkness and doubt we look
to the witnesses of faith.

76
00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:18.816
The father in Mark's Gospel
prayed an honest prayer

77
00:05:18.836 --> 00:05:23.824
that many of us know: I
believe; help my unbelief.

78
00:05:23.844 --> 00:05:26.363
That prayer is not failure.

79
00:05:26.383 --> 00:05:29.039
It is faith asking for help.

80
00:05:29.059 --> 00:05:34.665
Closer to home, Blessed Benedict
Daswa of Limpopo — a teacher and

81
00:05:34.685 --> 00:05:40.359
catechist — chose to trust Christ
even when it cost him his life.

82
00:05:40.379 --> 00:05:44.270
We will meet him properly
in later sessions.

83
00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:47.838
For now, let his
courage remind us that

84
00:05:47.858 --> 00:05:51.700
living faith can be
held even in the dark.

85
00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:59.176
Faith is personal:
each of us answers

86
00:05:59.196 --> 00:06:02.621
God freely and makes
the faith our own.

87
00:06:02.641 --> 00:06:05.139
Yet faith is never isolated.

88
00:06:05.159 --> 00:06:07.789
Believing is an ecclesial act.

89
00:06:07.809 --> 00:06:11.101
We say both I believe
and We believe.

90
00:06:11.121 --> 00:06:14.745
The Church is the
mother of all believers.

91
00:06:14.765 --> 00:06:17.792
No one walks alone into the Creed.

92
00:06:17.812 --> 00:06:22.032
We grow in faith together,
held by the prayer,

93
00:06:22.052 --> 00:06:26.160
teaching and witness of
the whole people of God.

94
00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.456
So here is the heart
of this session.

95
00:06:33.476 --> 00:06:37.013
Faith is our response
to the God who speaks.

96
00:06:37.033 --> 00:06:38.484
Hold on to him.

97
00:06:38.504 --> 00:06:40.079
Receive his truth.

98
00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:41.918
Grow with his Church.

99
00:06:41.938 --> 00:06:47.315
This week, read Genesis chapter
twelve and Luke's Annunciation again.

100
00:06:47.335 --> 00:06:53.079
Learn the first line of the Apostles'
Creed by heart: I believe in God,

101
00:06:53.099 --> 00:06:57.126
the Father almighty,
Creator of heaven and earth.

102
00:06:57.146 --> 00:07:03.258
And each night, pray that father's
prayer: I believe; help my unbelief.

103
00:07:03.278 --> 00:07:05.282
Thank you for listening.

104
00:07:05.302 --> 00:07:07.080
Join us on Thursday.
